    "narrative": "The Austin Waves lineup faces a daunting slate today, with several bats testing the lower end of our starting thresholds against elite arms like Ohtani and Fried. **Kyle Tucker** (65.86) stands as our strongest play; despite the matchup against a formidable southpaw, his base production and favorable slotting in the #5 hole secure his status as our primary engine. **Sam Antonacci** (60.17) also rates highly as a high-leverage start, bolstered by his lead-off status and a strong .391 xwOBA that gives him a tangible edge against Lugo. While **Gunnar Henderson** (60.37) battles a tough assignment against Fried, his park factor adjustment (+16%) and consistent top-of-order usage keep him locked into the core, even as his platoon metrics suffer.\n\nRegarding our bench decisions, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (50.94) represents our most difficult exclusion. While his raw talent is superior to several active starters, he sits today due to a convergence of factors: a sub-3.00 xERA matchup against an elite arm and a negative platoon differential that suppressed his efficiency score below the levels of our projected starters. We remain cautious with **Heliot Ramos** (43.69), who faces the toughest matchup of the day against Ohtani; his score is perilously close to our \"Below Floor\" threshold. We are also monitoring the availability of **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg**, as their continued absence on the IL remains a significant drag on our ceiling in the stolen base and total production categories.\n\nThe primary risk today is the reliance on hitters facing high-skill arms, which necessitates a strict focus on efficiency to avoid burning game caps on sub-optimal performances. We are relying on **Andy Pages** (59.99) and **Liam Hicks** (59.93) to outperform their base projections, as both benefit from dynamic platoon advantages that help offset the risks posed by their respective opponents. With our roster depth tested, we continue to look for value in **Nasim Nunez** and **Coby Mayo**; their lower scores serve as a reminder that we are prioritizing daily efficiency in a 5x5 Roto format where every plate appearance counts toward our cumulative average and speed totals.",
